    {
      "id": "8701366c6daa17d6b58fbd44ca7b2688ef4733a9",
      "tag": "autogenerated:ai-review",
      "author": {
        "_account_id": 1345,
        "name": "Gerrit AI review for Lustre",
        "display_name": "AI review",
        "email": "gaireview@linuxhacker.ru",
        "username": "aireview",
        "status": "Contact Oleg Drokin (green@whamcloud.com) with any questions on this account"
      },
      "date": "2026-11-06 14:05:09.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(3 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nSome concerns. The patch does stop the LU-21120 failure, but the new gate turns test_32b into an unconditional skip rather than an interop skip. Every client that runs this copy of sanityn.sh is >= 2.17.55, since 2.15.0, 2.16.0 and 2.17.0 all still carry `#run_test 32b`. Any older client that did run it would fail the same way, because clients stopped setting LDLM_FL_DENY_ON_CONTENTION in 2.14.53. Would it be cleaner to finish what 5ad00e36ec (\"LU-14838 osc: Remove client contention support\") started, and delete test_32b (or at least restore the disabled run_test) instead of keeping a gate that cannot pass?",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    },
