          "date": "2026-11-05 07:25:10.000000000",
          "tz": 480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21120 tests: skip sanityn test_32b on interop clients",
        "message": "LU-21120 tests: skip sanityn test_32b on interop clients\n\nsanityn test_32b measures lockless I/O, which is only entered after\nthe server returns -EUSERS in response to LDLM_FL_DENY_ON_CONTENTION.\nThe test guard checks only OST1_VERSION, so an old server plus a new\nclient runs the test even though the new client does not set that\nflag and lockless_write_bytes stays zero.\n\nRequire both OST1_VERSION and CLIENT_VERSION to be older than 2.17.53\nbefore running the test. This preserves the existing old-server-only\ncoverage and skips the interop combination that cannot trigger the\nmeasured path.\n\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanityn\nFixes: 73f14d6c16d (\"LU-12550 ldlm: contention detection\")\nSigned-off-by: Xiyang Wang <xiwang@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: I528f16e34ea4f171aeba5e81a910fe42b223fa5b\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
